///
/// At least one of [text], [icon], and [child] must be non-null. The [text]
/// and [child] arguments must not be used at the same time. The
/// [iconMargin] is only useful when [icon] and either one of [text] or
/// [child] is non-null.␀␀’¥’,}’¥a/// The text to display as the tab's label.
///
/// Must not be used in combination with [child].␀“{’°€Ğ“{€­/// The widget to be used as the tab's label.
///
/// Usually a [Text] widget, possibly wrapped in a [Semantics] widget.
///
/// Must not be used in combination with [text].␀“Ã“‡@“Ã*/// An icon to display as the tab's label.␀•“ÎZ• /// The margin added around the tab's icon.
///
/// Only useful when used in combination with [icon], and either one of
